  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Implemented the guarded Sage 3D PlotSpec bridge in standalone commit 7472656c: plain Surface3d instances lower to rectangular surfaces, all-triangular Mesh3d instances lower to triangular meshes, and one convex planar polygon lowers to a polygon layer. Unsupported mesh/dots companions, nonrepresentable transforms, multi-face polygonal topology, and invalid single polygons preserve the exact raw Plotly fallback. Stable IDs, source provenance, bounds, diagnostics, explicit resource limits, native-disabled behavior, and Sage 10.9 differential fixtures are covered. The validated no-redundant-copy path, combined with root commit 8a2e2ce8, measured plotspec_ms=4544.865634 for a 300x300 surface versus about 32300 ms before optimization; the unchanged Plotly path measured 17.547439 ms.",
    "risks": [
      "The full integration tier remains red for unrelated pre-existing native artifact, multiprocessing, sparse-random timeout, and performance-threshold failures; every 2D/3D plotting integration test, including graphics3d and Sage surface coverage, passed in that run.",
      "The focused test is intentionally not registered in the central node test manifest because that file belongs to the integration lane."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
